# RViz2 Simulation Configuration
# This config file sets up RViz2 for Gazebo simulation visualization

# Default display setup:
# 1. RobotModel - shows the robot URDF model
# 2. LaserScan - shows LiDAR data
# 3. Axes - world reference
# 4. Grid - floor reference

# To use:
# 1. Launch Gazebo simulation: ros2 launch agenticros_bringup gazebo_sim_only.launch.py
# 2. Launch RViz: ros2 run rviz2 rviz2 -d path/to/simulation.rviz
# 3. Verify /scan topic is showing LiDAR data
# 4. Verify robot model is moving (if /cmd_vel is publishing)

# Window layout:
# - Top left: RobotModel (gray robot structure)
# - Top right: LaserScan (ranges from LiDAR)
# - Bottom left: Axes (world X=Red, Y=Green, Z=Blue)
# - Bottom right: Grid (floor plane)

# Topics configured:
# - RobotModel: robot_description topic
# - LaserScan: /scan (or /lidar_scan depending on configuration)
# - TF: shows coordinate frames (base_link, laser_link, odom, map)

# If using Nav2:
# - Add 'Pose With Covariance Stamped' to see robot pose
# - Add 'Path' to see planned trajectories

# Troubleshooting:
# - If robot model not visible: verify robot_state_publisher is running
# - If /scan not showing: check rplidar_node is publishing
# - If TF errors: verify all frames are publishing correctly